The bug is in `_last_line_hash` (C:/Users/bogda/Documents/YHWH-v2.4-full/YHWH v2.4/scripts/core/audit_log.py, lines 104-123), not in `verify_chain`. When the target monthly file does not exist yet (month rollover), `_last_line_hash` must look back at the most recently dated prior `*.ndjson` file in the same directory and return the sha256 of its last line. Only if no prior file exists should it fall back to `_CHAIN_GENESIS`.

Replace the body of `_last_line_hash` with:

```python
def _last_line_hash(path: Path) -> str:
    """ξ.17 SEC-005 — return the sha256 of the last line in `path`,
    or the sha256 of the last line of the most recent prior monthly file
    in the same directory, or ``_CHAIN_GENESIS`` if nothing exists."""
    if not path.is_file():
        # Month rollover: look for the most recent prior monthly file.
        siblings = sorted(path.parent.glob("*.ndjson"))
        # Exclude the target path itself (it doesn't exist) and take last.
        prior = [p for p in siblings if p != path]
        if prior:
            path = prior[-1]  # oldest-first sort; last = most recent prior month
        else:
            return _CHAIN_GENESIS
    try:
        text = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except OSError:
        return _CHAIN_GENESIS
    lines = [ln for ln in text.splitlines() if ln.strip()]
    if not lines:
        return _CHAIN_GENESIS
    return hashlib.sha256(lines[-1].encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()
```

This is additive and safe: `verify_chain` is unchanged; existing chains and build outputs are unaffected; the 9 KJV editions remain byte-stable. The fix only changes what `prev_hash` value is written into the first line of a new monthly file — making it chain back to the prior month's last line instead of genesis.

