The most complete fix per S7.1 is to add @lru_cache(maxsize=1) and correct the docstring. The function has no mutable runtime callers (canons.yaml is never written at runtime via any API endpoint), so no cache_clear() concern in production. Tests that exercise this path should call _canons_index.cache_clear() in their fixtures if they swap canons.yaml. The fix:

```python
@functools.lru_cache(maxsize=1)
def _canons_index() -> dict:
    """Load canons.yaml and return {canon_id: {label, description, books}}.
    Singleton cache (project-internal published data; S7.1): updates require
    a git commit + process restart, not a runtime reload.
    """
    canons_path = REPO / "content" / "canons.yaml"
    if not canons_path.is_file():
        return {}
    import yaml
    data = yaml.safe_load(canons_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")) or {}
    return data.get("canons", {}) or {}
```

